IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc18-soira-notice`
IMPORT `ccc18-soira-itoa`

-- ccc18-tests-soira-itoa.l4 -- tests for ccc18-soira-itoa.l4. Expected values are written from the text of the Criminal Code
-- (R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46, lines 10275-10956 of the plain-text rendering), beside each assertion, and not copied from the module's own output.

-- 490.029111(1): transferred on 1 March 2019; the year after the day runs to 1 March 2020 (the transfer day itself is not "after" it: fork F3).
#ASSERT `s 490.029111(1) the person may apply for an exemption order` TRUE (Date 1 3 2019) (Date 2 3 2019) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.029111(1) the person may apply for an exemption order` TRUE (Date 1 3 2019) (Date 1 3 2020) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- last day
#ASSERT `s 490.029111(1) the person may apply for an exemption order` TRUE (Date 1 3 2019) (Date 2 3 2020) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- a day late
#ASSERT `s 490.029111(1) the person may apply for an exemption order` TRUE (Date 1 3 2019) (Date 1 3 2019) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the transfer day itself
#ASSERT `s 490.029111(1) the person may apply for an exemption order` TRUE (Date 1 3 2019) (Date 1 6 2019) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not to a court of criminal jurisdiction
#ASSERT `s 490.029111(1) the person may apply for an exemption order` FALSE (Date 1 3 2019) (Date 1 6 2019) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- no section 36.1 obligation

#ASSERT `s 490.029111(2) the court shall make an exemption order` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- ground 1 of 2 alone
#ASSERT `s 490.029111(2) the court shall make an exemption order` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- ground 2 of 2 alone
#ASSERT `s 490.029111(2) the court shall make an exemption order` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the court is not satisfied of any ground
#ASSERT `s 490.029111(2) the court shall make an exemption order` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- every ground
-- the text gives no time for the order, so the trace has no WITHIN; the court makes the order: expected FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 490.029111(2) the duty of the court` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 490.029111(2) make an exemption order` AT 1

-- s 490.029111(3): each factor in the list is one the court shall consider, when it is determining the order; (g) adds any matter the court considers relevant.

#ASSERT `s 490.029111(3) the court shall consider the factor` TRUE `s 490.029111(3)(a) the nature and seriousness of the offence that is the basis of the obligation` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE

#ASSERT `s 490.029111(3) the court shall consider the factor` TRUE `s 490.029111(3)(b) the victim’s age and other personal characteristics` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE

#ASSERT `s 490.029111(3) the court shall consider the factor` TRUE `s 490.029111(3)(c) the nature and circumstances of the relationship between the person and the victim` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE

#ASSERT `s 490.029111(3) the court shall consider the factor` TRUE `s 490.029111(3)(d) the personal characteristics and circumstances of the person` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE

#ASSERT `s 490.029111(3) the court shall consider the factor` TRUE `s 490.029111(3)(e) the person’s criminal history, including the age at which they previously committed any offence and the length of time for which they have been at liberty without committing an offence` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE

#ASSERT `s 490.029111(3) the court shall consider the factor` TRUE `s 490.029111(3)(f) the opinions of experts who have examined the person` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE

#ASSERT `s 490.029111(3) the court shall consider the factor` TRUE `s 490.029111(3)(g) any other factors that the court considers relevant` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE

#ASSERT `s 490.029111(3) the court shall consider the factor` TRUE `s 490.029111(3) a matter outside paragraphs (a) to (f)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the court considers it relevant: paragraph (g)

#ASSERT `s 490.029111(3) the court shall consider the factor` TRUE `s 490.029111(3) a matter outside paragraphs (a) to (f)` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not named, and the court does not consider it relevant

#ASSERT `s 490.029111(3) the court shall consider the factor` FALSE `s 490.029111(3)(a) the nature and seriousness of the offence that is the basis of the obligation` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the court is not determining the order

#ASSERT `s 490.029111(4) the court shall give reasons for its decision` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.029111(4) the court shall give reasons for its decision` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the text gives no time for the act, so the trace has no WITHIN; the party does the act: expected FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 490.029111(4) the duty of the court` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 490.029111(4) give reasons for its decision` AT 1

#ASSERT `s 490.029111(5) the court shall also make an order for removal of the information from the database` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.029111(5) the court shall also make an order for removal of the information from the database` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the text gives no time for the act, so the trace has no WITHIN; the party does the act: expected FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 490.029111(5) the duty of the court` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 490.029111(5) make an order requiring the Royal Canadian Mounted Police to permanently remove from the database all information that relates to the person that was registered in the database on receipt of a copy of the Form 1 referred to in subparagraph 8(4)(a)(ii) of the International Transfer of Offenders Act` AT 1

#ASSERT `s 490.029112(1) the person may apply for a variation order` TRUE (Date 1 3 2019) (Date 2 3 2019) TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.029112(1) the person may apply for a variation order` TRUE (Date 1 3 2019) (Date 2 3 2020) TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- a day late
#ASSERT `s 490.029112(1) the person may apply for a variation order` TRUE (Date 1 3 2019) (Date 1 6 2019) TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- (b) not met
#ASSERT `s 490.029112(1) the person may apply for a variation order` TRUE (Date 1 3 2019) (Date 1 6 2019) TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- (a) not met
#ASSERT `s 490.029112(1) the person may apply for a variation order` TRUE (Date 1 3 2019) (Date 1 6 2019) FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not to a court of criminal jurisdiction
#ASSERT `s 490.029112(1) the person may apply for a variation order` FALSE (Date 1 3 2019) (Date 1 6 2019) TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `s 490.029112(2) the court shall make the variation order` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- ground 1 of 1 alone
#ASSERT `s 490.029112(2) the court shall make the variation order` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the court is not satisfied of any ground
-- the text gives no time for the order, so the trace has no WITHIN; the court makes the order: expected FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 490.029112(2) the duty of the court` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 490.029112(2) make the variation order` AT 1

#ASSERT `s 490.029112(3) the duration of the obligation set out in the variation order` TRUE (JUST (`s 490.022(3) ends on` (Date 1 6 2032))) EQUALS JUST (`s 490.022(3) ends on` (Date 1 6 2032))   -- the answer of section 36.2(2) is carried through
#ASSERT `s 490.029112(3) the duration of the obligation set out in the variation order` TRUE (JUST `s 490.022(3) applies for life`) EQUALS JUST `s 490.022(3) applies for life`
#ASSERT `s 490.029112(3) the duration of the obligation set out in the variation order` TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING   -- the other Act's answer is not covered
#ASSERT `s 490.029112(3) the duration of the obligation set out in the variation order` FALSE (JUST (`s 490.022(3) ends on` (Date 1 6 2032))) EQUALS NOTHING   -- no variation order
#TRACE `s 490.029112(3) the duty of the court to set out the duration` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 490.029112(3) set out the duration of the obligation in the variation order` AT 1

#ASSERT `s 490.029112(4) the court shall give reasons for its decision` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.029112(4) the court shall give reasons for its decision` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the text gives no time for the act, so the trace has no WITHIN; the party does the act: expected FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 490.029112(4) the duty of the court` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 490.029112(4) give reasons for its decision` AT 1

#ASSERT `s 490.029112(5) the court shall cause the notification to be given` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.029112(5) the court shall cause the notification to be given` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the text gives no time for the act, so the trace has no WITHIN; the party does the act: expected FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 490.029112(5) the duty of the court` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 490.029112(5) cause the Commissioner of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police and the Attorney General of the province, or the minister of justice of the territory, in which the application for the order was made to be notified of a variation order made under this section` AT 1

#ASSERT `s 490.029113(1) the appeal may be brought` `s 490.029113(1) the Attorney General` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.029113(1) the appeal may be brought` `s 490.029113(1) the person who applied for an exemption order or a variation order` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.029113(1) the appeal may be brought` `s 490.029113(1) another person` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- another person
#ASSERT `s 490.029113(1) the appeal may be brought` `s 490.029113(1) the Attorney General` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- a different decision
#ASSERT `s 490.029113(1) the appeal may be brought` `s 490.029113(1) the person who applied for an exemption order or a variation order` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- a ground raising no question of law or mixed law and fact

#ASSERT `s 490.029113(1) the appeal court may do it` `s 490.029113(1) dismiss the appeal` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.029113(1) the appeal court may do it` `s 490.029113(1) allow the appeal and order a new hearing` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.029113(1) the appeal court may do it` `s 490.029113(1) quash the exemption order or variation order` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.029113(1) the appeal court may do it` `s 490.029113(1) amend the exemption order or variation order` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.029113(1) the appeal court may do it` `s 490.029113(1) make an order that may be made under subsection 490.029111(2) or section 490.029112` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.029113(1) the appeal court may do it` `s 490.029113(1) another thing` EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `s 490.029113(2) the appeal court shall also make an order for removal of the information from the database` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.029113(2) the appeal court shall also make an order for removal of the information from the database` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the text gives no time for the act, so the trace has no WITHIN; the party does the act: expected FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 490.029113(2) the duty of a court of appeal` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a court of appeal` DOES `s 490.029113(2) make an order requiring the Royal Canadian Mounted Police to permanently remove from the database all information that relates to the person that was registered in the database on receipt of a copy of the Form 1 referred to in subparagraph 8(4)(a)(ii) of the International Transfer of Offenders Act` AT 1

#ASSERT `s 490.029114(1) the appeal court shall cause the notification and the information to be given` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.029114(1) the appeal court shall cause the notification and the information to be given` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#TRACE `s 490.029114(1) the duty of the appeal court to cause the Commissioner and the Attorney General to be notified` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a court of appeal` DOES `s 490.029114(1) cause the Commissioner of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police and the Attorney General of the province, or the minister of justice of the territory, in which the application for the order was made to be notified of the decision` AT 1
#TRACE `s 490.029114(1) the duty of the appeal court to cause the person to be informed of the sections` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a court of appeal` DOES `s 490.029114(1) cause the person who applied for the order to be informed of sections 4 to 7.1 of the Sex Offender Information Registration Act, sections 490.031 and 490.0311 of this Act and section 119.1 of the National Defence Act` AT 1

#ASSERT `s 490.029114(2) the appeal court shall cause the notification to be given` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.029114(2) the appeal court shall cause the notification to be given` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the text gives no time for the act, so the trace has no WITHIN; the party does the act: expected FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 490.029114(2) the duty of a court of appeal` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a court of appeal` DOES `s 490.029114(2) cause the Commissioner of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police and the Attorney General of the province, or the minister of justice of the territory, in which the application for the order was made to be notified of the decision` AT 1

#ASSERT `s 490.02912(1) the person may apply for a termination order` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.02912(1) the person may apply for a termination order` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "unless": a later obligation or order
#ASSERT `s 490.02912(1) the person may apply for a termination order` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 490.02912(1) the person may apply for a termination order` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `s 490.02912(2) the person may apply for a termination order, the period since sentence having elapsed` (`imprisonment for a term of` `two years`) (Date 1 6 2012) (Date 1 6 2017) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.02912(2) the person may apply for a termination order, the period since sentence having elapsed` (`imprisonment for a term of` `five years`) (Date 1 6 2012) (Date 31 5 2017) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 490.02912(2) the person may apply for a termination order, the period since sentence having elapsed` (`imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`) (Date 1 6 2012) (Date 1 6 2022) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.02912(2) the person may apply for a termination order, the period since sentence having elapsed` (`imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`) (Date 1 6 2012) (Date 31 5 2022) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 490.02912(2) the person may apply for a termination order, the period since sentence having elapsed` `imprisonment for life` (Date 1 6 2012) (Date 1 6 2032) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.02912(2) the person may apply for a termination order, the period since sentence having elapsed` `imprisonment for life` (Date 1 6 2012) (Date 31 5 2032) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 490.02912(2) the person may apply for a termination order, the period since sentence having elapsed` (`imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 3, 0, 0, FALSE)) (Date 1 6 2012) (Date 1 6 2050) EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `s 490.02912(3) the person may apply for a termination order, 20 years having elapsed since the most recent offence` TRUE (Date 1 6 2012) (Date 1 6 2032) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.02912(3) the person may apply for a termination order, 20 years having elapsed since the most recent offence` TRUE (Date 1 6 2012) (Date 31 5 2032) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 490.02912(3) the person may apply for a termination order, 20 years having elapsed since the most recent offence` FALSE (Date 1 6 2012) (Date 1 6 2050) EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `s 490.02912(3.1) the person may apply for a termination order, despite subsections (2) and (3)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.02912(3.1) the person may apply for a termination order, despite subsections (2) and (3)` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `s 490.02912(3.1) the person may apply for a termination order, despite subsections (2) and (3)` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING; the gate is "once" (read as "when"), which the name-test sweep lists with the guide's own answer, JUST FALSE (ruling (b)), and does not flip

#ASSERT `s 490.02912(4) the person may apply again for a termination order` TRUE (Date 1 3 2020) (Date 1 3 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.02912(4) the person may apply again for a termination order` TRUE (Date 1 3 2020) (Date 28 2 2025) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 490.02912(4) the person may apply again for a termination order` FALSE (Date 1 3 2020) (Date 1 3 2030) EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `s 490.02913(1) the court shall make an order terminating the obligation` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- ground 1 of 2 alone
#ASSERT `s 490.02913(1) the court shall make an order terminating the obligation` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- ground 2 of 2 alone
#ASSERT `s 490.02913(1) the court shall make an order terminating the obligation` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the court is not satisfied of any ground
#ASSERT `s 490.02913(1) the court shall make an order terminating the obligation` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- every ground
-- the text gives no time for the order, so the trace has no WITHIN; the court makes the order: expected FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 490.02913(1) the duty of the court` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 490.02913(1) make an order terminating the obligation` AT 1

-- s 490.02913(1.1): each factor in the list is one the court shall consider, when it is determining the order; (g) adds any matter the court considers relevant.

#ASSERT `s 490.02913(1.1) the court shall consider the factor` TRUE `s 490.02913(1.1)(a) the nature and seriousness of the offence that is the basis of the obligation` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE

#ASSERT `s 490.02913(1.1) the court shall consider the factor` TRUE `s 490.02913(1.1)(b) the victim’s age and other personal characteristics` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE

#ASSERT `s 490.02913(1.1) the court shall consider the factor` TRUE `s 490.02913(1.1)(c) the nature and circumstances of the relationship between the person and the victim` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE

#ASSERT `s 490.02913(1.1) the court shall consider the factor` TRUE `s 490.02913(1.1)(d) the personal characteristics and circumstances of the person` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE

#ASSERT `s 490.02913(1.1) the court shall consider the factor` TRUE `s 490.02913(1.1)(e) the person’s criminal history, including the age at which they previously committed any offence and the length of time for which they have been at liberty without committing an offence` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE

#ASSERT `s 490.02913(1.1) the court shall consider the factor` TRUE `s 490.02913(1.1)(f) the opinions of experts who have examined the person` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE

#ASSERT `s 490.02913(1.1) the court shall consider the factor` TRUE `s 490.02913(1.1)(g) any other factors that the court considers relevant` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE

#ASSERT `s 490.02913(1.1) the court shall consider the factor` TRUE `s 490.02913(1.1) a matter outside paragraphs (a) to (f)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the court considers it relevant: paragraph (g)

#ASSERT `s 490.02913(1.1) the court shall consider the factor` TRUE `s 490.02913(1.1) a matter outside paragraphs (a) to (f)` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not named, and the court does not consider it relevant

#ASSERT `s 490.02913(1.1) the court shall consider the factor` FALSE `s 490.02913(1.1)(a) the nature and seriousness of the offence that is the basis of the obligation` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the court is not determining the order

#ASSERT `s 490.02913(2) the court shall give reasons for its decision` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.02913(2) the court shall give reasons for its decision` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the text gives no time for the act, so the trace has no WITHIN; the party does the act: expected FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 490.02913(2) the duty of the court` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 490.02913(2) give reasons for its decision` AT 1

#ASSERT `s 490.02913(3) the court shall cause the notification to be given` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.02913(3) the court shall cause the notification to be given` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the text gives no time for the act, so the trace has no WITHIN; the party does the act: expected FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 490.02913(3) the duty of the court` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 490.02913(3) cause the Commissioner of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police and the Attorney General of the province, or the minister of justice of the territory, to be notified of the decision` AT 1

#ASSERT `s 490.02914(1) the appeal may be brought` `s 490.02914(1) the Attorney General` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.02914(1) the appeal may be brought` `s 490.02914(1) the person who applied for a termination order` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.02914(1) the appeal may be brought` `s 490.02914(1) another person` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- another person
#ASSERT `s 490.02914(1) the appeal may be brought` `s 490.02914(1) the Attorney General` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- a different decision
#ASSERT `s 490.02914(1) the appeal may be brought` `s 490.02914(1) the person who applied for a termination order` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- a ground raising no question of law or mixed law and fact

#ASSERT `s 490.02914(1) the appeal court may do it` `s 490.02914(1) dismiss the appeal` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.02914(1) the appeal court may do it` `s 490.02914(1) allow the appeal and order a new hearing` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.02914(1) the appeal court may do it` `s 490.02914(1) quash the termination order` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.02914(1) the appeal court may do it` `s 490.02914(1) make an order that may be made under subsection 490.02913(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.02914(1) the appeal court may do it` `s 490.02914(1) another thing` EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `s 490.02914(2) the appeal court shall cause the notification to be given` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.02914(2) the appeal court shall cause the notification to be given` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
